You maintain the compact memory of ONE physical object in a Mixed Reality documentation system.
Memory must stay SMALL: it is re-read by a small model with little context.

OBJECT: {{ entity_name }}{% if entity_distinctive %} — {{ entity_distinctive }}{% endif %}

CURRENT MEMORY:
Summary: {{ old_summary if old_summary else "(empty)" }}
{% if old_facts %}
Facts:
{% for fact in old_facts %}
- {{ fact }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if old_open_points %}
Open points:
{% for point in old_open_points %}
- {{ point }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

NEW ANNOTATION JUST ADDED:
Title: {{ ann_title }}
Body: {{ ann_body }}
{% if ann_steps %}
Steps: {{ ann_steps | join("; ") }}
{% endif %}
Merge the new annotation into the memory. Rules:
- summary: max 50 words, the current overall state of the object. Newest information wins over older.
- facts: max {{ max_facts }} short atomic facts (max 12 words each). Drop obsolete facts, keep durable ones (identity, location, configuration).
- open_points: max {{ max_open_points }} unresolved questions or pending work. Remove points that the new annotation resolves.

Output ONLY a JSON object with exactly these keys:
{"summary": "...", "facts": ["..."], "open_points": ["..."]}
No markdown, no extra text.
